Fixed content visibility under RBAC: content uploaded into a domain but not yet in any
repository (orphan content) was hidden from the domain's own members. The content access
policy now lists content by the domain-scoped ``core.view_content`` permission (held by
domain members via ``service.domain_admin``) instead of scoping by repository, so members
can view their orphan content on both the generic and typed content endpoints.

Also fixed a related read regression where a caller with no role on a ``public-*`` domain
received 404 when retrieving or listing its repositories or content; the public-domain read
bypass is now honoured in ``scope_queryset`` as well as ``has_permission``.

Hardened authorization for the domain create and migrate endpoints. Both are plain
``APIView`` s, so their ``DEFAULT_ACCESS_POLICY`` never ran and was misleading dead config.
They now use ``IsAuthenticated``, and domain migration additionally enforces an explicit
``core.change_domain`` object-level check. Domain-create request context (principal and org
id) is now reset after each request so a failed create can no longer leak into the next
request handled by the same worker.
